  "description": "SQL cells for ClrKernel: run T-SQL against one or more Microsoft SQL Server connections from a notebook, with results rendered as an interactive grid. Connections are named and secrets are kept out of committed files — passwords resolve from the OS credential store (macOS Keychain, Windows Credential Manager, Linux libsecret) or a pluggable secret provider. Drives the `#!sql` cell language across the Jupyter kernel, the JSON-RPC server, and the headless runner; connection and bulk-load mechanics live in ClrKernel.Database.Provider.SqlServer.",
